From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: panic if the link to the NVMe disk is lost on
 resume

The system runs from its NVMe disk. If the link to it doesn't come back,
the reset that follows the resume fails, and blk_mark_disk_dead() shuts
down ext4 on /data and /metadata. Userspace is left running without them,
and nvme_suspend() returns -EBUSY for the dead controller, so the system
can't suspend either. Nothing in the kernel reboots it: ext4 stops
reporting errors once it is shut down, so errors=panic wouldn't fire.

Panic instead once the retry has failed, so that the system restarts on
its own after CONFIG_PANIC_TIMEOUT. Do it here rather than from the NVMe
driver, which would only find out by reading CSTS through the BAR of the
dead link. That access isn't guarded, and what it does on this SoC hasn't
been measured.

Do the same if the host can't be initialized at all, which leaves the
controller unclocked. Limit this to links that were up at suspend with an
NVMe device behind them. A lost Wi-Fi link or an empty slot doesn't panic
here, what happens next is up to the driver of the device.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
index 4431bdff1..dbcd360bb 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
@@ -1299,6 +1299,34 @@ int dw_pcie_suspend_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(dw_pcie_suspend_noirq);
 
+static int dw_pcie_find_nvme(struct pci_dev *pdev, void *data)
+{
+	bool *found = data;
+
+	if (pdev->class == PCI_CLASS_STORAGE_EXPRESS)
+		*found = true;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The system runs from the NVMe disk. Restart now, before anything below the
+ * Root Port is resumed: only the config accesses are guarded against a dead
+ * link, the BARs aren't.
+ */
+static void dw_pcie_resume_link_lost(struct dw_pcie *pci)
+{
+	bool nvme = false;
+
+	if (!pci->link_up_at_suspend)
+		return;
+
+	pci_walk_bus(pci->pp.bridge->bus, dw_pcie_find_nvme, &nvme);
+	if (nvme)
+		panic("%s: link to the NVMe disk lost on resume\n",
+		      dev_name(pci->dev));
+}
+
 int dw_pcie_resume_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 {
 	bool retry = pci->link_up_at_suspend;
@@ -1312,6 +1340,7 @@ int dw_pcie_resume_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 		ret = pci->pp.ops->init(&pci->pp);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(pci->dev, "Host init failed: %d\n", ret);
+			dw_pcie_resume_link_lost(pci);
 			return ret;
 		}
 	}
@@ -1340,6 +1369,9 @@ int dw_pcie_resume_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 		goto bring_up;
 	}
 
+	if (ret)
+		dw_pcie_resume_link_lost(pci);
+
 	/*
 	 * The PM core resumes the Root Port and its children whatever happens
 	 * here, and they reach the controller through the DBI. Keep the host
